videos.script:
Until now the planner ran from a project folder. Nobody else has that folder. {{folder}}

What they get is a package, and every system has its own kinds. {{formats}} One of them, Android's bundle, cannot even be installed by a person.

Every package needs an icon, in a dozen sizes. You draw one, and a tool cuts the rest. {{icon}}

Then Electron's packages. The first build lands in the wrong folder, and the second one refuses to finish. {{builder}} Both are worth reading, because both say exactly what is missing.

Then the packages opened up: what is inside, and what each one asks the computer for. {{inside}}

And last, the phone packages this machine could not build, and a checklist that runs before any of them. {{checklist}}
